/**
 * The glyphs the shipped components need, as path data.
 *
 * **This package has no icon dependency and is not getting one.** A design system that forces a
 * particular icon library on a host is one a host cannot use; the React edition depends on Radix's
 * icons only because it already did. So the glyphs our own components name are the paths themselves,
 * copied from the same Radix set React renders, and a host's own icons are components it passes.
 *
 * **15×15 is not a detail.** The framework-neutral stylesheet sizes an icon chip with
 * `svg[width="15"], .vui-icon`, so a glyph at any other intrinsic size renders at the
 * replaced-element default and the chip around it looks broken, which is how an earlier wave shipped
 * an oversized OTP icon.
 */
